From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mt76 npu reorder the mt7916 rx in mt76

mt76_rx_poll_complete skips the mt76 reorder buffer whenever a wed or
an npu is active, on the assumption that the hardware below reorders.
Neither does here: the airoha wed is tx only (no rx capability) and the
MT7916 has no hardware reorder, while its NPU passes the frames on as
they come unless it is told the ba windows.  Without a reorder the
aggregated rx reached the stack out of order.

Handing the windows to the NPU (experimental/0110) held a client's
uplink for 50..100 ms several times a second under a download, even
with the block ack requests forwarded.  Keep the windows in the mt76
reorder buffer instead: skip it only for a wed with rx and for an npu
whose driver does not ask for the host reorder, and ask for it on the
mt7916.

Signed-off-by: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mac80211.c
+++ b/mac80211.c
@@ -1663,8 +1663,14 @@
 
 	while ((skb = __skb_dequeue(&dev->rx_skb[q])) != NULL) {
 		mt76_check_sta(dev, skb);
-		if (mtk_wed_device_active(&dev->mmio.wed) ||
-		    mt76_npu_device_active(dev))
+		/* leave the reorder to the hardware only where it
+		 * does it: a wed with rx, an npu that orders the
+		 * frames itself.  the airoha wed is tx only and the
+		 * mt7916 npu passes the frames as they come. */
+		if ((mtk_wed_device_active(&dev->mmio.wed) &&
+		     mtk_wed_get_rx_capa(&dev->mmio.wed)) ||
+		    (mt76_npu_device_active(dev) &&
+		     !dev->mmio.npu_host_reorder))
 			__skb_queue_tail(&frames, skb);
 		else
 			mt76_rx_aggr_reorder(skb, &frames);
--- a/mt76.h
+++ b/mt76.h
@@ -736,6 +736,8 @@
 	struct airoha_npu __rcu *npu;
 	phys_addr_t phy_addr;
 	int npu_type;
+	/* the npu passes the frames unordered: mt76 reorders them */
+	bool npu_host_reorder;
 };
 
 struct mt76_rx_status {
--- a/mt7915/npu.c
+++ b/mt7915/npu.c
@@ -224,6 +224,10 @@
 {
 	int err;
 
+	/* the mt7916 has no hardware reorder and the npu is not told
+	 * about the ba windows: mt76 keeps the reorder buffer */
+	dev->mt76.mmio.npu_host_reorder = is_mt7916(&dev->mt76);
+
 	mutex_lock(&dev->mt76.mutex);
 	err = __mt7915_npu_hw_init(dev);
 	mutex_unlock(&dev->mt76.mutex);
